 11	# Fix Proposal: Add Do Session Scanning to `GetAllConsiliumSessions`
 12	
 13	## Root Cause Reference
 14	
 15	The root cause is documented in [phase-07.md](../phase-07.md#6-root-cause-analysis): `GetAllConsiliumSessions()` in `session.handler.ts` never scans `~/.consilium/do_sessions/`.
 16	
 17	## Proposed Changes
 18	
 19	### 1. Add `listDoSessions()` to `session.handler.ts`
 20	
 21	**File:** `C:/Users/zemuro/Antigravity/kimi_extension_mod/src/handlers/session.handler.ts`
 22	
 23	Add a new function after `listThinkSessions()` (line 82):
 24	
 25	```typescript
 26	async function listDoSessions(): Promise<SessionInfo[]> {
 27	  const dir = path.join(os.homedir(), ".consilium", "do_sessions");
 28	  console.log("[session.handler] listDoSessions dir:", dir, "exists:", fs.existsSync(dir));
 29	  if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) return [];
 30	  const entries = await fs.promises.readdir(dir, { withFileTypes: true });
 31	  const sessions: SessionInfo[] = [];
 32	  for (const e of entries) {
 33	    if (!e.isDirectory() || !UUID_REGEX.test(e.name)) continue;
 34	    const journalPath = path.join(dir, e.name, "journal.jsonl");
 35	    if (!fs.existsSync(journalPath)) continue;
 36	    const st = await fs.promises.stat(journalPath);
 37	    // Do sessions don't embed a user message in the journal;
 38	    // use an excerpt of the work_dir as the display title.
 39	    const brief = await getFirstEntryWorkDir(journalPath) || DEFAULT_FALLBACK_TITLE;
 40	    sessions.push({
 41	      id: e.name,
 42	      workDir: brief, // work_dir from journal entry
 43	      updatedAt: st.mtimeMs || st.mtime.getTime(),
 44	      contextFile: journalPath,
 45	      brief,
 46	      isThinking: false,
 47	    });
 48	  }
 49	  return sessions.sort((a, b) => b.updatedAt - a.updatedAt);
 50	}
 51	
 52	/** Read the work_dir from the first session_start entry of a Do session journal. */
 53	async function getFirstEntryWorkDir(journalPath: string): Promise<string | null> {
 54	  try {
 55	    const lines = (await fs.promises.readFile(journalPath, "utf-8")).split("\n");
 56	    for (const line of lines) {
 57	      if (!line.trim()) continue;
 58	      try {
 59	        const entry = JSON.parse(line);
 60	        if (entry.type === "session_start" && entry.work_dir) {
 61	          return entry.work_dir;
 62	        }
 63	      } catch { continue; }
 64	    }
 65	  } catch { /* ignore */ }
 66	  return null;
 67	}
 68	```
 69	
 70	### 2. Wire it into `GetAllConsiliumSessions`
 71	
 72	**File:** `C:/Users/zemuro/Antigravity/kimi_extension_mod/src/handlers/session.handler.ts`
 73	
 74	In the `[Methods.GetAllConsiliumSessions]` handler, add a Do session scan block after the Think session scan (after line 132, before the sort on line 134):
 75	
 76	```typescript
 77	// Also surface Do sessions (not scanned by SDK or Think scanner)
 78	for (const s of await listDoSessions()) {
 79	  if (!seen.has(s.id)) {
 80	    seen.add(s.id);
 81	    const meta = ctx.getSessionMetadata(s.id);
 82	    s.brief = meta?.title || s.brief;
 83	    (s as any).mode = meta?.mode || 'do';
 84	    allSessions.push(s);
 85	  }
 86	}
 87	```
 88	
 89	### 3. Update `SessionInfo` type to include `isThinking: false` for Do sessions
 90	
 91	No change needed — the `SessionInfo` interface already has `isThinking: boolean`. Do sessions should have `isThinking: false`, which is what the proposed `listDoSessions()` does.
 92	
 93	### 4. Frontend
 94	
 95	No frontend changes needed. `SessionList.tsx` already renders a `ModeBadge` for `mode: 'do'`.
 96	
 97	## Edge Cases & Risks
 98	
 99	| Edge case | Mitigation |
100	|-----------|------------|
101	| Do session directory exists but `journal.jsonl` is empty | `getFirstEntryWorkDir` returns null; fall back to `DEFAULT_FALLBACK_TITLE` |
102	| Do session has no `session_start` entry | Same fallback |
103	| Corrupted `journal.jsonl` | try/catch — entry is skipped gracefully |
104	| `do_sessions/` directory doesn't exist | `fs.existsSync` check returns early |
105	| Case-insensitive UUID collision (very unlikely) | `seen` set deduplicates by ID, same as Think sessions |
106	| Do session titles are less informative than Think titles | Use `work_dir` as title; user can rename via the existing rename feature |
107	
108	## Alternative Approach Considered
109	
110	Add `listDoSessions()` to the SDK (`agent_sdk/storage.ts`) and export it alongside `listSessions()` and `listThinkSessions()`. This would keep the listing logic centralized but requires rebuilding the npm package. The proposed approach keeps the fix isolated to the extension handler, is simpler, and can be implemented without a package rebuild.
111	
112	## Effort Estimate
113	
114	| Task | Time |
115	|------|------|
116	| Add `listDoSessions()` function | 0.5h |
117	| Wire into `GetAllConsiliumSessions` | 0.25h |
118	| Test with existing Do sessions | 0.5h |
119	| Verify frontend renders Do badges correctly | 0.25h |
120	| **Total** | **1.5h** |
121	
122	## Recommendation
123	
124	Implement this as part of Phase 08 (or rename Phase 07 to include the fix). The investigation is complete and the fix is small — ~15 lines of new code, no frontend changes, no SDK rebuild.

  1	import * as vscode from "vscode";
  2	import * as path from "node:path";
  3	import * as fs from "fs";
  4	import * as os from "node:os";
  5	import { Methods, Events } from "../../shared/bridge";
  6	import {
  7	  listSessions,
  8	  listSessionsForWorkspace,
  9	  getRegisteredWorkDirs,
 10	  parseSessionEvents,
 11	  deleteSession,
 12	  forkSession,
 13	} from "@consilium/agent-sdk";
 14	import { BaselineManager } from "../managers";
 15	import {
 16	  DEFAULT_FALLBACK_TITLE,
 17	  deriveTitleFromSessionLines,
 18	} from "../lib/session-title";
 19	import type { SessionInfo, StreamEvent, ForkSessionResult } from "@consilium/agent-sdk";
 20	import type { Handler } from "./types";
 21	import { handlerLog } from "../utils/logger.js";
 22	
 23	const UUID_REGEX = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;
 24	
 25	interface LoadHistoryParams {
 26	  consiliumSessionId: string;
 27	  workDir?: string;
 28	}
 29	
 30	interface DeleteSessionParams {
 31	  sessionId: string;
 32	}
 33	
 34	interface ForkSessionParams {
 35	  sessionId: string;
 36	  turnIndex: number;
 37	}
 38	
 39	interface WriteSessionMetadataParams {
 40	  sessionId: string;
 41	  title: string;
 42	  source: "user" | "llm" | "fallback";
 43	}
 44	
 45	function getThinkDir(): string {
 46	  return path.join(os.homedir(), ".consilium", "think_sessions");
 47	}
 48	
 49	async function getFirstUserMessageFromThinkFile(filePath: string): Promise<string | null> {
 50	  try {
 51	    const lines = (await fs.promises.readFile(filePath, "utf-8")).split("\n");
 52	    return deriveTitleFromSessionLines(lines);
 53	  } catch {
 54	    return null;
 55	  }
 56	}
 57	
 58	async function listThinkSessions(): Promise<SessionInfo[]> {
 59	  const dir = getThinkDir();
 60	  console.log("[session.handler] listThinkSessions dir:", dir, "exists:", fs.existsSync(dir));
 61	  if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) return [];
 62	  const entries = await fs.promises.readdir(dir, { withFileTypes: true });
 63	  const sessions: SessionInfo[] = [];
 64	  for (const e of entries) {
 65	    if (!e.isDirectory() && e.name.endsWith(".jsonl")) {
 66	      const id = e.name.slice(0, -".jsonl".length);
 67	      if (!UUID_REGEX.test(id)) continue;
 68	      const filePath = path.join(dir, e.name);
 69	      const st = await fs.promises.stat(filePath);
 70	      const brief = (await getFirstUserMessageFromThinkFile(filePath)) || DEFAULT_FALLBACK_TITLE;
 71	      sessions.push({
 72	        id: id,
 73	        workDir: "[Think]",
 74	        updatedAt: st.mtimeMs || st.mtime.getTime(),
 75	        contextFile: filePath,
 76	        brief,
 77	        isThinking: true
 78	      });
 79	    }
 80	  }
 81	  return sessions.sort((a, b) => b.updatedAt - a.updatedAt);
 82	}
 83	
 84	export const sessionHandlers: Record<string, Handler<any, any>> = {
 85	  [Methods.GetConsiliumSessions]: async (_, ctx) => {
 86	    if (!ctx.workDir) return [];
 87	    const sessions = await listSessions(ctx.workDir);
 88	    for (const s of sessions) {
 89	      const meta = ctx.getSessionMetadata(s.id);
 90	      s.brief = meta?.title || s.brief;
 91	      (s as any).mode = meta?.mode || 'legacy';
 92	    }
 93	    return sessions;
 94	  },
 95	
 96	  [Methods.GetAllConsiliumSessions]: async (_, ctx) => {
 97	    if (!ctx.workspaceRoot) return [];
 98	
 99	    // The SDK hashes workDir case-sensitively. On Windows the same folder can
100	    // appear under c:\ and C:\ hashes. Query every registered variant.
101	    const registered = getRegisteredWorkDirs(ctx.workspaceRoot);
102	    const allSessions: SessionInfo[] = [];
103	    const seen = new Set<string>();
104	
105	    for (const dir of registered) {
106	      try {
107	        const sess = await listSessions(dir);
108	        for (const s of sess) {
109	          if (!seen.has(s.id)) {
110	            seen.add(s.id);
111	            const meta = ctx.getSessionMetadata(s.id);
112	            s.brief = meta?.title || s.brief;
113	            (s as any).mode = meta?.mode || 'legacy';
114	            allSessions.push(s);
115	          }
116	        }
117	      } catch {
118	        // ignore missing directories
119	      }
120	    }
121	
122	    // Also surface Think sessions (not scanned by SDK)
123	    for (const s of await listThinkSessions()) {
124	      if (!seen.has(s.id)) {
125	        seen.add(s.id);
126	        const meta = ctx.getSessionMetadata(s.id);
127	        // Keep the first-message brief unless the user set a custom title.
128	        s.brief = meta?.title || s.brief;
129	        (s as any).mode = meta?.mode || 'think';
130	        allSessions.push(s);
131	      }
132	    }
133	
134	    return allSessions.sort((a, b) => b.updatedAt - a.updatedAt);
135	  },
136	
137	  [Methods.GetRegisteredWorkDirs]: async (_, ctx) => {
138	    return ctx.workspaceRoot ? getRegisteredWorkDirs(ctx.workspaceRoot) : [];
139	  },
140	
141	  [Methods.SetWorkDir]: async (params: { workDir: string | null }, ctx) => {
142	    if (!ctx.workspaceRoot) {
143	      return { ok: false };
144	    }
145	    const target = params.workDir;
146	    if (target && target !== ctx.workspaceRoot && !target.startsWith(ctx.workspaceRoot + path.sep)) {
147	      return { ok: false };
148	    }
149	    ctx.setCustomWorkDir(target);
150	    return { ok: true, workDir: target || ctx.workspaceRoot };
151	  },
152	
153	  [Methods.BrowseWorkDir]: async (_, ctx) => {
154	    if (!ctx.workspaceRoot) {
155	      return { ok: false, workDir: null };
156	    }
157	    const workspaceUri = vscode.Uri.file(ctx.workspaceRoot);
158	    let subdirs: string[] = [];
159	    try {
160	      const entries = await vscode.workspace.fs.readDirectory(workspaceUri);
161	      subdirs = entries
162	        .filter(([, type]) => type === vscode.FileType.Directory)
163	        .map(([name]) => name)
164	        .filter((name) => !name.startsWith("."))
165	        .sort();
166	    } catch {
167	      // Ignore errors
168	    }
169	
170	    const items: vscode.QuickPickItem[] = [
171	      { label: "$(folder) Browse...", description: "Open folder picker", alwaysShow: true },
172	      { label: "", kind: vscode.QuickPickItemKind.Separator },
173	      ...subdirs.map((name) => ({
174	        label: `$(folder) ${name}`,
175	        description: path.join(ctx.workspaceRoot!, name),
176	      })),
177	    ];
178	
179	    const picked = await vscode.window.showQuickPick(items, {
180	      placeHolder: "Select a subdirectory or browse...",
181	      title: "Working Directory",
182	    });
183	
184	    if (!picked) {
185	      return { ok: false, workDir: null };
186	    }
187	
188	    let selected: string;
189	    if (picked.label === "$(folder) Browse...") {
190	      const result = await vscode.window.showOpenDialog({
191	        canSelectFiles: false,
192	        canSelectFolders: true,
193	        canSelectMany: false,
194	        defaultUri: workspaceUri,
195	        openLabel: "Select Working Directory",
196	      });
197	      if (!result || result.length === 0) {
198	        return { ok: false, workDir: null };
199	      }
200	      selected = result[0].fsPath;
201	    } else {
202	      selected = picked.description!;
203	    }
204	
205	    if (selected !== ctx.workspaceRoot && !selected.startsWith(ctx.workspaceRoot + path.sep)) {
206	      vscode.window.showWarningMessage("Selected directory must be within the workspace.");
207	      return { ok: false, workDir: null };
208	    }
209	
210	    ctx.setCustomWorkDir(selected === ctx.workspaceRoot ? null : selected);
211	    return { ok: true, workDir: selected };
212	  },
213	
214	  [Methods.LoadConsiliumSessionHistory]: async (params: LoadHistoryParams, ctx): Promise<StreamEvent[]> => {
215	    if (!UUID_REGEX.test(params.consiliumSessionId)) {
216	      return [];
217	    }
218	
219	    const thinkFile = path.join(getThinkDir(), `${params.consiliumSessionId}.jsonl`);
220	    const isThinkFile = fs.existsSync(thinkFile);
221	
222	    // Think sessions can be loaded without a workspace; Do sessions require one.
223	    if (!isThinkFile && !ctx.workDir) {
224	      return [];
225	    }
226	
227	    const fileKey = ctx.getFileManagerKey();
228	    ctx.fileManager.setSessionId(fileKey, params.consiliumSessionId);
229	    if (ctx.workDir) {
230	      BaselineManager.initSession(ctx.workDir, params.consiliumSessionId);
231	    }
232	
233	    // ---- Think session path (base history) ----
234	    const thinkEvents: StreamEvent[] = [];
235	    if (isThinkFile) {
236	      const lines = (await fs.promises.readFile(thinkFile, "utf-8"))
237	        .split("\n")
238	        .filter((l) => l.trim());
239	      for (const line of lines) {
240	        try {
241	          const entry = JSON.parse(line);
242	          if (entry.role === "user" || entry.role === "assistant") {
243	            thinkEvents.push({
244	              type: "Message",
245	              payload: { role: entry.role, content: entry.content },
246	              _sessionId: params.consiliumSessionId,
247	              mode: 'think',
248	            } as any);
249	          }
250	        } catch {
251	          // ignore malformed lines
252	        }
253	      }
254	    }
255	
256	    const meta = ctx.getSessionMetadata(params.consiliumSessionId);
257	    // If a think file exists and the stored mode is not explicitly 'do', treat it as a Think session.
258	    // This protects against lost globalState after extension reinstall.
259	    const mode = meta?.mode || (isThinkFile ? 'think' : 'legacy');
260	    const resolvedMode: 'think' | 'do' = mode === 'do' ? 'do' : 'think';
261	
262	    if (resolvedMode === 'think') {
263	      // Force terminal event so Think tab doesn't get stuck
264	      thinkEvents.push({
265	        type: "history_restored",
266	        result: { status: "restored" },
267	        _sessionId: params.consiliumSessionId,
268	        mode: 'think',
269	      } as any);
270	      return thinkEvents;
271	    }
272	
273	    // ---- Regular Do session path ----
274	    // Prefer the workDir supplied by the caller; fall back to registered
275	    // variants to handle Windows case-sensitivity differences.
276	    let doEvents: StreamEvent[] = [];
277	    const candidateWorkDirs = new Set<string>();
278	    if (params.workDir) candidateWorkDirs.add(params.workDir);
279	    if (ctx.workDir) candidateWorkDirs.add(ctx.workDir);
280	    if (ctx.workspaceRoot) {
281	      for (const dir of getRegisteredWorkDirs(ctx.workspaceRoot)) {
282	        candidateWorkDirs.add(dir);
283	      }
284	    }
285	    if (candidateWorkDirs.size === 0) {
286	      return [];
287	    }
288	    for (const dir of candidateWorkDirs) {
289	      try {
290	        const events = await parseSessionEvents(dir, params.consiliumSessionId);
291	        if (events.length > 0) {
292	          doEvents = events;
293	          break;
294	        }
295	      } catch {
296	        // try next candidate
297	      }
298	    }
299	
300	    const events = [
301	      ...thinkEvents,
302	      ...doEvents.map((e) => ({ ...e, _sessionId: params.consiliumSessionId, mode: 'do' as const }) as any),
303	    ];
304	
305	    // If the previous CLI process was killed (window reload), wire.jsonl ends
306	    // mid-stream. The webview would stay stuck in isProcessing=true.
307	    // Append a history_restored event to unlock the UI.
308	    if (!ctx.getTurn()) {
309	      const last = events[events.length - 1] as any;
310	      const isTerminal =
311	        last &&
312	        (last.type === "stream_complete" ||
313	          last.type === "stream_aborted" ||
314	          last.type === "history_restored" ||
315	          last.type === "error" ||
316	          last.type === "turn_complete" ||
317	          last.type === "done");
318	      if (!isTerminal) {
319	        events.push({
320	          type: "history_restored",
321	          result: { status: "restored" },
322	          _sessionId: params.consiliumSessionId,
323	          mode: 'do',
324	        } as any);
325	      }
326	    }
327	
328	    return events;
329	  },
330	
331	  [Methods.DeleteConsiliumSession]: async (params: DeleteSessionParams, ctx): Promise<{ ok: boolean }> => {
332	    if (!ctx.workDir || !UUID_REGEX.test(params.sessionId)) {
333	      return { ok: false };
334	    }
335	    return { ok: await deleteSession(ctx.workDir, params.sessionId) };
336	  },
337	
338	  [Methods.ForkConsiliumSession]: async (params: ForkSessionParams, ctx): Promise<ForkSessionResult | null> => {
339	    if (!ctx.workDir || !UUID_REGEX.test(params.sessionId) || params.turnIndex < 0) {
340	      return null;
341	    }
342	    try {
343	      return await forkSession({
344	        workDir: ctx.workDir,
345	        sourceSessionId: params.sessionId,
346	        turnIndex: params.turnIndex,
347	      });
348	    } catch (err) {
349	      handlerLog.error("Fork session failed", { error: String(err) });
350	      return null;
351	    }
352	  },
353	
354	  [Methods.WriteSessionMetadata]: async (params: WriteSessionMetadataParams, ctx) => {
355	    const { sessionId, title, source } = params;
356	    const meta = ctx.getSessionMetadata(sessionId) ?? {};
357	    ctx.setSessionMetadata(sessionId, {
358	      ...meta,
359	      title,
360	      titleSource: source,
361	      titleGeneratedAt: source === "llm" ? Date.now() : meta.titleGeneratedAt,
362	    });
363	    ctx.broadcast(
364	      Events.SessionTitleUpdated,
365	      { sessionId, title, source },
366	      ctx.webviewId,
367	    );
368	    return { ok: true };
369	  },
370	
371	  [Methods.RestoreTabState]: async (_, ctx) => {
372	    return ctx.getRestoredTabState();
373	  },
374	};
